    "body": "My suggestion is to include a table similar to the one attached; for describing all the percent encode sets, as well as error correction and validation for all individual code points in percent-encoded components. \n\nKey:\n\n- v: valid\n- E: (Escape) valid but nonetheless percent encoded\n- T: (Tolerte) invalid, but nonetheless left untouched by the parser -- resulting in an invalid URL as output\n- F: (Fixed) invalid and fixed by parser (and setters) by percent encoding the occurrence\n- R: (Reject) Invalid and causing a hard error, won't end up in output URLs.\n\nThe apostrophe in the query is special cased for 'non-special' URLs where it is left untouched (ie. v:valid)\n\n'Other control' here includes unicode non-chars and surrogates.\n\nI do hope the table is fully up to date, I have not checked if there have been any recent changes.\n\n<img width=\"603\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c6576764-2954-4050-b993-0266e5162302\" />",
